do GameState.learn_fact("j_past_adventures")
do GameState.start_minigame()
audio music "res://audio/Character Sounds/main menu backtrack 2.wav" [volume="-5.0" loop="true"]
[background arg="res://assets/Locations/Abandoned_Silver_Mine.png" fade="1.0" transition="Push Up"]
join Juniper (Animated) left
join Lizzy (Animated) right [extra_data="show Side"]
join Foreground (Tv Overlay Mm) center [animation="Fade In" length="0.8" wait="true" z_index="1"]
[wait time="1.5"]
VO: Come on, Lizzy. Everything has led to this.
VO: She’s your best friend.
VO: Piece of cake.
label Journal Select
do MenuManager.open_journal()
[wait_input]
if {is_success} == true:
	do MinegameTest.update_background("strikes_number")
	if {current_item} == "j_past_adventures":
		Lizzy: Back in the diner, when we all shared our favourite Vermilion Hills weird moment, I couldn’t choose.
		Lizzy: and you called it a cop out, but it’s true.
		Lizzy: I wouldn’t trade any of them for the world.
		Juniper: ...
		Lizzy: the good.
		Lizzy: the bad.
		Lizzy: the sort of okay, but not really remarkable moments too.
		Lizzy: all the times I was kinda like, is this really necessary?
		Juniper: None of it really matters.
		Juniper: You may think you’ve had a choice in everything, that you you made mistakes and learned from them...
		Juniper: but you didn’t.
		Juniper: Not really.
		Lizzy: All of those experiences made us who we are!
		Lizzy: Who I am.
		Lizzy: We can face anything life throws at us,
		Lizzy: We’ve faced evil magicians and demons,
		Lizzy: and oh my god, we survived high school??
		Lizzy: while juggling monsters every week and also powers and evil vampires trying to kill us.
		Juniper: You’re not getting it.
		Lizzy: I do get it.
		Lizzy: I’m terrified of the future. I would give anything to keep everything exactly the same.
		Lizzy: But this isn’t living, Jay.
		Lizzy: it’s having the same conversations over and over and over again. Experiencing the same stupid math exam.
		Lizzy: That sounds incredibly lonely.
		Juniper: ...
		Juniper: You have no idea.

	
	elif {current_item} == "noah":
		join Noah center
		Noah: Come on, Juniper. You’re like, the second most chill person I know. Other than me of course.
		Noah: if you keep looping us, we’ll never get to try out deep fried ice cream.
		Noah: like, how does the ice cream not immediately melt?
		Juniper: ...
		Juniper: it’s coated in batter—
		Noah: Yeah, I know, but it’s like, who figured that out?
		Noah: like did this accidentally drop ice cream in the vat of oil and then it turned out okay?
		Noah: accidents and unexpected miracles!
		Noah: can’t get that in a time loop.
		Juniper: ...
		Juniper: and mars bars.
		Juniper: Don’t forget mars bars.
		Noah: and mars bars!
		Noah: like, what?!
		leave Noah
	
	elif {current_item} == "barb":
		join Barb center
		Barb: Juniper, you know you’re acting super totally not okay right?
		Barb: like supervillain levels of not okay.
		Juniper: I know it seems like that, Barb, but this is all for a very good reason—
		Barb: Save the rationalizing crap for someone who doesn’t know you and how incredibly and infuriating compassionate you are.
		Barb: Like, everything you do and say drives me up the damn wall,
		Barb: because I’m like, she’s figuring it out.
		Barb: she’s doing the right thing.
		Barb: You find the perfect nice thing to say every time and make it look so effortless. Like saint levels of nice.
		Juniper: Well, I wouldn’t go that far...
		Barb: Take the compliment. Being emotionally vulnerable isn’t easy for me, okay?
		Juniper: Thank you.
		Barb: You’re welcome.
		Barb: But also.
		Barb: Why are you acting like such an idiot?
		Barb: Don’t you know how important you are?
		Barb: Get it together!!
		Juniper: ...
		Juniper: Barb...
		leave Barb
	
	
	elif {current_item} == "valerie":
		join Valerie center
		Valerie: The only reason that you are taking this course of action is because you feel it necessary.
		Valerie: and even with your clairvoyance, you do not know what the future holds.
		Valerie: seeing a single piece of an impossibly large picture...
		Valerie: you can’t possibly know all of the context.
		Juniper: I’ve seen enough, Valerie.
		Valerie: this ritual you’ve created, looping the same day over and over again, is from a place of uncertainty, which is completely normal for someone your age.
		Valerie: You may feel in control, but this time loop is trapping you just as much as it’s trapping us.
		Valerie: There is no winning.
		Valerie: no gaming the system.
		Valerie: You must see that. Don’t ignore that feeling of fear.
		Valerie: We will face it together.
		Juniper: ...
		leave Valerie
	
	elif {current_item} == "knightmare":
		join Knightmare center
		Knightmare: You are a powerful psychic and a formidable foe. I’ve always deeply respected you out of all the annoying children.
		Juniper: ...
		Juniper: uh.
		Juniper: thanks?
		Knightmare: Do not mistake this for a compliment, it means I must slay you in battle to truly succeed.
		Knightmare: but that is for another time.
		...
		Juniper: ... okay?
		Knightmare: we have destinies to attend to, young one.
		Knightmare: for the past several decades I lived in my Julian’s shadow, thinking it was the only way forward, when it was holding me back.
		Knightmare: Once you shed the false impression of the life you deserve,
		Knightmare: you can become who you were truly meant to be.
		Juniper: I do have to say, this knight look suits you way better than Lady MacBeth.
		Juniper: far less derivative.
		Knightmare: You are an intelligent woman.
		Knightmare: Perhaps, when this is all over...
		Knightmare: What would you say if I offered a position as my second in command?
		Lizzy: Okay, wait, hang on—
		Juniper: um.
		join Dagger offright
		Dagger: my... Lady?
		Knightmare: oh do shut up right now, Dagger, can’t you see the goth and I are having a tender moment?
		Lizzy: you consider this tender?
		Lizzy: Stop recruiting my morally confused friend!
		...
		leave Dagger
		leave Knightmare
	
	elif {current_item} == "dagger":
		join Dagger center
		Dagger: Juniper,
		Dagger: Lizzy has shared with me how much she cares for you.
		Dagger: How much you support your friends. Your family. Your town.
		...
		Dagger: You are a protector.
		Juniper: I’m really not.
		Dagger: Do not downplay your role.
		Dagger: Lizzy may be the one in the prophecy, but you are equally as important.
		Juniper: My role is to support her.
		Juniper: Out of everyone, I would think you’d understand that.
		Dagger: Before I became what I am now,
		Dagger: I had very close friends, not to dissimilar to your group.
		Dagger: I would give up all of this realm, my immortal life, to go back to them, to see them one last time.
		Dagger: but I know I can’t, so I must continue on for them.
		Dagger: Do not destroy your friendships in an attempt to preserve them.
		Dagger: Treasure the few moments you do have,
		Dagger: because one day, you’ll look back fondly, and regret not doing more.
		Juniper: I think this situation is a little different,
		Dagger: What is immortality if not reliving the same moment over and over again?
		...
		leave Dagger
	
	elif {current_item} == "j_bffs":
		update Lizzy (Full Wolf)
		Lizzy: When I first moved here, you were the one that made me feel welcomed.
		Lizzy: You were the one that helped me deal with my werewolf stuff.
		Lizzy: Never once did I think you weren’t being genuine.
		Lizzy: You’re my best friend, Juniper.
		Lizzy: Without you...
		Lizzy: I wouldn’t be Lizzy Springs.
		Lizzy: Monster Hunter and Werewolf.
		Lizzy: I don’t care if we’re in a TV show or if we’re going to be hit by a meteor tomorrow.
		Lizzy: And if I have to chose between you or continuing on like this,
		Lizzy: In an endless loop of a badly written episode of television,
		Lizzy: Well,
		Lizzy: I’d choose you every time.
		Lizzy: Because I’d rather spend whatever time we have left with you,
		Lizzy: Even if that means just one more episode.
	
	set {strikes_number} += 1.0
	join "Strike Ball" leftmost [animation="Zoom In" length="9.0"]
	leave "Strike Ball" [animation="Slide To Right" length="1.1" wait="true"]
	if {strikes_number} == 1.0:
		join Minigame (1C) center
	elif {strikes_number} == 2.0:
		update Minigame (2c) center
	elif {strikes_number} == 3.0:
		update Minigame (3c) center
	elif {strikes_number} == 4.0:
		update Minigame (4c) center
	elif {strikes_number} == 5.0:
		update Minigame (5c) center
	elif {strikes_number} == 6.0:
		update Minigame (6c) center
		Juniper: You guys don’t understand.
		Juniper: If I end this,
		Juniper: There won’t be any more Vermilion Hills.
		Lizzy: What are you talking about?
		Juniper: This isn’t real.
		Juniper: We aren’t real.
		Juniper: We’re in a TV show called Lizzy Springs Monster Hunter and Werewolf,
		Juniper: And after this episode...
		Juniper: There’s nothing.
		join Valerie righter
		Valerie: Hm.
		leave Valerie
		join Barb offright
		Barb: Um, I think I’d  know if we were in a TV show.
		leave Barb
		Juniper: I’ve been rewinding the season, keeping us one episode before the finale.
		Juniper: If you stop me now, you’ll be killing everyone.
		join Knightmare midleft
		Knightmare: Rewinding the tape?
		Knightmare: Psychic tall one, how do you go about doing such a thing?
		Lizzy: Please don’t be getting any ideas, Knightmare.
		...
		leave Knightmare
		do GameState.learn_fact("j_bffs")
	[wait time="1.5"]
else:
	Juniper: There's no point in trying to stop me.
set {is_success} = false
if {strikes_number} < 7.0:
	jump Journal Select
update Minigame (7c) [animation="Tada" length="0.3" wait="true" repeat="5"]
join "black screen" center [animation="Instant In" z_index="2"]

[background fade="0.0"]
audio music - [fade="4.0"]
leave --All-- [animation="Instant Out"]
jump ending_7/